# 低频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List06核心词汇

grudge /ɡrʌdʒ/ n. 怨恨 She bore no grudge against her former rival. 她对以前的对手没有怨恨。
habitat /ˈhæbɪtæt/ n. 栖息地 Deforestation destroys natural habitats. 森林砍伐破坏了自然栖息地。
hail /heɪl/ v. 称赞 The innovation was hailed as a breakthrough. 该创新被誉为一项突破。
hazard /ˈhæzəd/ n. 危险 Chemical waste poses a serious environmental hazard. 化学废物构成严重的环境危害。
hemisphere /ˈhemɪsfɪə(r)/ n. 半球 Climate change affects both hemispheres. 气候变化影响两个半球。
herald /ˈherəld/ v. 预示 The discovery heralded a new era of research. 该发现预示着研究的新时代。
hierarchy /ˈhaɪərɑːki/ n. 层级 The organization has a rigid hierarchy. 该组织有严格的层级结构。
hospitable /hɒˈspɪtəbl/ adj. 好客的 The local community was very hospitable. 当地社区非常好客。
hostage /ˈhɒstɪdʒ/ n. 人质 The hostages were safely rescued. 人质被安全救出。
hover /ˈhɒvə(r)/ v. 盘旋 Unemployment rates hover around 5%. 失业率徘徊在5%左右。
humiliate /hjuːˈmilieɪt/ v. 羞辱 The team was humiliated in the final match. 该队在决赛中被羞辱。
hurdle /ˈhɜːdl/ n. 障碍 Funding remains the biggest hurdle. 资金仍然是最大的障碍。
hygiene /ˈhaɪdʒiːn/ n. 卫生 Personal hygiene is essential for public health. 个人卫生对公共健康至关重要。
hypocritical /ˌhɪpəˈkrɪtɪkl/ adj. 虚伪的 It would be hypocritical to preach tolerance while being intolerant. 宣扬容忍而不容忍是虚伪的。
illicit /ɪˈlɪsɪt/ adj. 非法的 The police cracked down on illicit drug trade. 警方打击了非法毒品交易。
immerse /ɪˈmɜːs/ v. 沉浸 She immersed herself in learning the new language. 她沉浸于学习新语言中。
imminent /ˈɪmɪnənt/ adj. 即将来临的 A major policy change is imminent. 一项重大政策变化即将来临。
impartial /ɪmˈpɑːʃəl/ adj. 公正的 The investigation must be conducted by an impartial body. 调查必须由公正的机构进行。
impede /ɪmˈpiːd/ v. 阻碍 Bureaucratic red tape impedes economic growth. 繁文缛节阻碍了经济增长。
impetus /ˈɪmpɪtəs/ n. 推动力 The crisis provided the impetus for reform. 危机为改革提供了推动力。
imprison /ɪmˈprɪzn/ v. 关押 He was imprisoned for his political beliefs. 他因政治信仰被关押。
incite /ɪnˈsaɪt/ v. 煽动 The speech incited the crowd to violence. 演讲煽动人群实施暴力。
incumbent /ɪnˈkʌmbənt/ adj. 现任的 The incumbent government faces strong opposition. 现任政府面临强烈反对。
incur /ɪnˈkɜː(r)/ v. 招致 The project incurred massive cost overruns. 项目招致了大量成本超支。
indemnity /ɪnˈdemnəti/ n. 赔偿 The insurance policy provides indemnity against property damage. 保险单提供财产损失赔偿。
indict /ɪnˈdaɪt/ v. 起诉 The grand jury indicted the suspect on multiple charges. 大陪审团以多项罪名起诉了嫌疑人。
indifferent /ɪnˈdɪfərənt/ adj. 漠然的 The government seemed indifferent to public concerns. 政府似乎对公众关切漠不关心。
inflict /ɪnˈflɪkt/ v. 造成 The earthquake inflicted widespread damage. 地震造成了大面积破坏。
inhabit /ɪnˈhæbɪt/ v. 栖息 The island is inhabited by a rare species of bird. 该岛栖息着一种稀有鸟类。
inhibit /ɪnˈhɪbɪt/ v. 抑制 High interest rates inhibit investment. 高利率抑制了投资。
